    slug: "devops-32-how-stateful-sets-differ-from-deployements",
    shortDescription: "[REPORTED] Reported interview question/topic from the supplied source.",
    sampleAnswer: "A Deployment is generally used for stateless replicated\nworkloads where interchangeable Pods are acceptable. A StatefulSet is\ndesigned for workloads that need stable identities, stable network\nnames, and often persistent storage associations. StatefulSet Pods have\npredictable ordinal identities and are managed with ordering semantics\nthat differ from a Deployment. Databases are a common example, although\nwhether Kubernetes should run a particular database depends on\noperational requirements.",
