    sampleAnswer: "Terraform state maps the resources declared in configuration to\nreal infrastructure and records attributes Terraform needs to plan\nchanges. For teams, state should normally be stored in a secure remote\nbackend with appropriate access control and state locking where\nsupported. If state is lost, do not blindly recreate resources: first\npreserve the configuration and infrastructure, recover state from\nbackend/versioned backups if available, or reconstruct state by\nimporting existing resources. Secrets can also appear in state, so state\nrequires security controls.",
